comment.narrative:
The travel time on all the project's built or rehabilitated infrastructure has decreased from 44.83 min to 33.86 min on average, a reduction of 24.47% against a target of 50%.

The reasons for not achieving the target have to do with the installation of several safety measures on all the roads rehabilitated or built, including traffic lights, speed bumps and also the high use of infrastructure. 

The travel times obtained after the traffic survey are:   
- Airport drive: 2.38 min or 33% reduction;
- Balmer route: 5.44 min or 29% reduction; 
- Tolakouadiokro road: 7.42 min or 13% reduction; 
- Crossing BouakE by the A3: 12.61 min or 24.5% reduction;
- Voie Rond-point CHR at the Cargill crossroads: 0.58 min or 33.1% reduction; 
- Rue des Grumiers: 5.43 min or 15.1% reduction;
